--- NOTE on the two responsiveness probes (not part of the finding, required by the gate) ---
The first instrumented gate run of this task failed "The main actor answers while the conversation index
is being read" and "The engine answers a state request while a document is converting": both sampled the
main actor once, at 200 ms and 600 ms, and this task's transport tests added enough main-actor work to
miss that sample. Neither test is weakened — each now waits for the same flag with a bounded 5-second
poll, and the semaphore that holds the read open is still released only after that wait, so on the code
they were written to catch the flag never appears and they still fail. Both pass in 0.04 s now instead of
sleeping out their sample. For the same reason the ring test uses `#require` for the length it is about to
index: with the "one slot instead of a ring" mutation it used to trap (`Fatal error: Index out of range`)
rather than fail, and a test that crashes takes the process with it.

